{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19214" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨1,-1,1⟩$ and $q=⟨8,4,2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-19214" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{p\\cdot p}p \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}⟨1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-19214" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d93e2ccd72089ed0873c0eea0f1986f63c3af93623471f4bf5ddca4fc4974d62"} {"question" "q-19214" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-19214" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-2,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,-3,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,-6,6⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-19214" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,-2,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-126510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-126510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+0\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{4}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}d \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-126510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d93e2ccd72089ed0873c0eea0f1986f63c3af93623471f4bf5ddca4fc4974d62"} {"question" "q-126510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-126510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,3,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,6,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},1,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{4}{3},2,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-126510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-212459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,-1,-2⟩$ and $b=⟨x,-4,0⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-212459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x+4 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-212459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d93e2ccd72089ed0873c0eea0f1986f63c3af93623471f4bf5ddca4fc4974d62"} {"question" "q-212459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-212459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-212459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $q=⟨4,8,2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q=⟨$  \n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{p\\cdot p}p \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 8+1\\cdot 2}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}⟨-1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d93e2ccd72089ed0873c0eea0f1986f63c3af93623471f4bf5ddca4fc4974d62"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-275232" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨5,-3,4⟩$ and $b=⟨1,2,-2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5-6-8}{1+4+4}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{9}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d93e2ccd72089ed0873c0eea0f1986f63c3af93623471f4bf5ddca4fc4974d62"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039093/state.json" "file_sha256" "74dc465f0097fc3f1077567be69c213fe7a4f8448d5894ac1d5194a5e79217dd"} {"question" "q-317652" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "